WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:29.916


2
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.250
<b>Here, Arjuna,</b>

3
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:36.041
<b>Here, Arjuna’s request for</b>
<b>Lord Krishna, his charioteer,</b>

4
00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:39.208
<b>to be driven to the center of the battlefield</b>
<b>is elaborated upon.</b>

5
00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:40.458
<b>He says, </b>

6
00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.916
<b>Evil-minded Duryodhana's well-wishing kings,</b>

7
00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:48.333
<b>who have assembled here on this battlefield,</b>

8
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.625
<b>I desire to see them all.</b>

9
00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:55.500


10
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.083
<b>Arjuna is a bit enraged here.</b>

11
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:04.041
<b>He calls Duryodhana the evil,</b>
<b>the wicked-minded son of Dhritarashtra. </b>

12
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:07.125
<b>Fraudulently seizing the Pandavas' rights, </b>

13
00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:10.333
<b>insulting every peace offering, </b>

14
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:12.458
<b>attempting to kill the Pandavas, </b>

15
00:01:12.458 --> 00:01:15.125
<b>forcibly disrobing Draupadi</b>
<b>in the crowded assembly </b>

16
00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:17.041
<b>Duryodhana has, not once </b>

17
00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:22.166
<b>but many times, given proof of his</b>
<b>demonic tendencies to everyone.</b>

18
00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:23.416
<b>Seeing all this, </b>

19
00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>knowing all this, </b>

20
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.458
<b>still so many kings have come</b>
<b>to side with Duryodhana. </b>

21
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:30.208
<b>Isn't it astonishing?</b>

22
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:31.083
<b>But </b>

23
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.958
<b>only he can do such a thing, </b>

24
00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.416
<b>who is himself of polluted mind, </b>

25
00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:37.041
<b>an evildoer. </b>

26
00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:41.166
<b>And how can Arjuna</b>
<b>not be furious at such kings?</b>

27
00:01:41.791 --> 00:01:46.000


28
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.833
<b>Arjuna's anger is natural. </b>

29
00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:53.541
<b>It's also natural to think that </b>

30
00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:59.041
<b>all the kings siding with Duryodhana</b>
<b>are unrighteous, </b>

31
00:01:59.041 --> 00:02:01.666
<b>followers of sin.</b>

32
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:03.708
<b>But</b>

33
00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:05.583
<b>there are also a few people,</b>

34
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.250
<b>A few Kings,</b>

35
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.041
<b>who are compelled</b>

36
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:12.083
<b>to stand with Duryodhana,</b>

37
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:19.333
<b>perhaps burdened by an old debt</b>
<b>or a favor.</b>

38
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>Or some</b>

39
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:28.416
<b>whom Duryodhana has ensnared</b>
<b>by invoking friendship. </b>

40
00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:31.041
<b>The reason may be compulsion. </b>

41
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:32.500
<b>But</b>

42
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.625
<b>all of them will have to bear the consequences.</b>

43
00:02:37.625 --> 00:02:40.625
<b>Whoever enters a chamber filled with coal</b>

44
00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:44.166
<b>will emerge stained with soot.</b>

45
00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:49.958
<b>Such is the effect of bad company.</b>

46
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:52.583
<b>The people you associate with,</b>

47
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:54.375
<b>befriend,</b>

48
00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:56.041
<b>jest with</b>

49
00:02:56.041 --> 00:03:02.375
<b>their influence inevitably begins</b>
<b>to affect your life.</b>

50
00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:07.791
<b>Even if a black stain falls</b>
<b>just once on white clothes,</b>

51
00:03:07.791 --> 00:03:11.291
<b>it becomes difficult to remove.</b>

52
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.458
<b>But</b>

53
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:16.541
<b>the consequences of a taint</b>
<b>on one's sacred character</b>

54
00:03:16.541 --> 00:03:22.500
<b>is impossible to escape without suffering them</b>

55
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.416
<b>Be mindful of yourself.</b>

56
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:29.125


57
00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.625
<b>Man is a familial being;</b>

58
00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:34.333
<b>he lives in a family.</b>

59
00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:37.750
<b>He is also a social being.</b>

60
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.000
<b>Being part of some group is his inherent need,</b>

61
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.250
<b>be it a circle of friends,</b>

62
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.666
<b>a religious sect,</b>

63
00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:51.125
<b>or a regional party.</b>

64
00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:53.791
<b>In such situations, staying united</b>

65
00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:58.375
<b>and helping each other is good.</b>

66
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.500
<b>Because what a group can accomplish,</b>

67
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.625
<b>an individual alone cannot.</b>

68
00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:08.458
<b>There is immense power in unity.</b>

69
00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:12.458
<b>Now, if the work is good, </b>

70
00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:14.291
<b>it benefits everyone,</b>

71
00:04:14.291 --> 00:04:16.541
<b>benefits society.</b>

72
00:04:16.541 --> 00:04:19.375
<b>But</b>

73
00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:21.791
<b>the dilemma is</b>

74
00:04:21.791 --> 00:04:23.541
<b>that in a family or a group, </b>

75
00:04:23.541 --> 00:04:30.791
<b>some people blindly go along,</b>

76
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:33.833
<b>offering support even if the work is bad.</b>

77
00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:39.708
<b>Does an individual's duty</b>
<b>towards the group</b>

78
00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:44.208
<b>become just to go along even in bad deeds? </b>

79
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:45.916
<b>No, right?</b>

80
00:04:45.916 --> 00:04:47.916
<b>Towards a family </b>

81
00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:50.791
<b>Or a group, it’s our responsibility, to reason.</b>

82
00:04:50.791 --> 00:04:54.166
<b>To understand </b>

83
00:04:54.166 --> 00:04:57.458
<b>good and bad, </b>

84
00:04:57.458 --> 00:04:59.750
<b>and to make others understand too.</b>

85
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.291
<b>Stopping someone else from doing wrong</b>

86
00:05:02.291 --> 00:05:06.583
<b>is also a social responsibility, isn't it?</b>

87
00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:10.750
<b>And suppose no one listens to you.</b>

88
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.041
<b>Even then,</b>

89
00:05:12.041 --> 00:05:14.291
<b>by keeping yourself away from bad deeds,</b>

90
00:05:14.291 --> 00:05:18.583
<b>you have reduced evil to some extent. </b>

91
00:05:18.583 --> 00:05:19.958
<b>Even if small, </b>

92
00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:24.916
<b>you have contributed to society in this too.</b>

93
00:05:24.916 --> 00:05:28.333
<b>At the most basic level, what is society? </b>

94
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:30.958
<b>It is one individual.</b>

95
00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:33.833
<b>You yourself are society. </b>

96
00:05:34.458 --> 00:05:38.583


97
00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:40.500
<b>There are many kings, </b>

98
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.041
<b>who are deliberately supporting Duryodhana. </b>

99
00:05:46.041 --> 00:05:51.791
<b>Right or wrong, Pandavas or Kauravas.</b>
<b>They don’t really care about all that.</b>

100
00:05:51.791 --> 00:05:53.958
<b>All they can only see, </b>

101
00:05:53.958 --> 00:05:56.416
<b>is their self-interest.</b>

102
00:05:56.416 --> 00:05:58.000
<b>There are also some who, </b>

103
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.333
<b>due to their personal bitterness</b>
<b>towards the Pandavas, </b>

104
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:08.250
<b>are strengthening their enemy -Duryodhana.</b>

105
00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.041
<b>This is what they call </b>

106
00:06:11.041 --> 00:06:13.666
<b>Politics.</b>

107
00:06:13.666 --> 00:06:16.458
<b>Professional politics...</b>

108
00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:20.916
<b>you must have heard this term. </b>

109
00:06:20.916 --> 00:06:22.833
<b>You must have seen it, </b>

110
00:06:22.833 --> 00:06:24.125
<b>perhaps </b>

111
00:06:24.125 --> 00:06:28.625
<b>even been a part of it. </b>

112
00:06:28.625 --> 00:06:32.125
<b>No one benefits from it.</b>

113
00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:37.083
<b>Sooner or later, this habit brings one down.</b>

114
00:06:37.083 --> 00:06:39.958
<b>And why even engage in all this? </b>

115
00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:44.791
<b>Do you not have faith in your own capability?</b>

116
00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:51.083
<b>It's best to stay away from these schemes.</b>

117
00:06:51.083 --> 00:06:54.541
<b>All these paths will eventually lead to dead ends. </b>

118
00:06:54.541 --> 00:06:58.291
<b>It's just not visible now.</b>

119
00:06:58.291 --> 00:07:02.541
<b>Your work alone will work for you. </b>

120
00:07:02.541 --> 00:07:04.208
<b>Hear it again </b>

121
00:07:04.208 --> 00:07:07.708
<b>your work alone will work for you.</b>

122
00:07:07.708 --> 00:07:11.166
<b>And if you have to give time,</b>

123
00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:15.166
<b>give it to improving your competence.</b>

124
00:07:15.166 --> 00:07:18.708
<b>That is the certain path to progress.</b>

